WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:54.300
<b>Unprecedented</b>

3
00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.930
Gomorrah!

4
00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.650
[FAMILY MAN]
What are you doing? You're gonna knock us off
if you keep crashing like that!

5
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.980
Whoa! Maybe he's too injured to go on!

6
00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.650
What? No!

7
00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.120
Gomorrah can't see!

8
00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.060
His retinas were
damaged in that last attack!

9
00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:18.190
He's blind!

10
00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:21.840
What's that?

11
00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:22.650
Gomorrah!

12
00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:24.150
You can't see anything?

13
00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.750
[OFFICIAL]
It started running like crazy!

14
00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:30.720
[MARINE]
Don't just stand there!

15
00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:31.420
Shoot it!

16
00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:32.690
We gotta stop that thing!

17
00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.100
[OFFICIAL]
We can't let it go any further!

18
00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.930
Fire the trench mortars!

19
00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.690
[MOZU]
Gomorrah, don't do this!

20
00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:40.430
Please stop!

21
00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.130
[KIWI]
You're in no shape to go on!

22
00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:43.730
You'll kill yourself!

23
00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:50.110
[CHOPPER]
He said that he made
a promise to Sodom.

24
00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:55.040
He told Sodom "Leave the rest to me!"

25
00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:59.050
"I'll take on your share and carry
everyone the rest of the way!"

26
00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:02.020
Gomorrah.

27
00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:08.140
[FRANKY]
They were in its stomach?

28
00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:11.440
I'm full already...couldn't
eat another bite.

29
00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:14.440
Let's take 'em with us as back-up food.

30
00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:18.080
Big Bro! Come here, quick!

31
00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:21.550
Some pirates gave Sodom and
Gomorrah a serious beating!

32
00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.880
You pirates have got a lotta nerve!

33
00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.680
Never touch my family!

34
00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:32.260
[FRANKY]
Hey!

35
00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.820
Take it easy, you two!

36
00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:35.290
You're still injured!

37
00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.530
This is no time for a dance party!

38
00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:43.080
Look!

39
00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:43.780
[FAMILY MAN]
We're headed straight for a dead end!

40
00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.390
He'll crash into it and die!

41
00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:47.460
[ZAMBAI]
Gomorrah! Stop it!

42
00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.860
You'll never make it! Stop!

43
00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:53.730
[ZORO]
A dead end?

44
00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:54.700
I don't see one.

45
00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:55.430
Do you?

46
00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:56.730
Nope.

47
00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.900
[SANJI]
Can't say I see anything of the sort.

48
00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:36.580
It's the Courthouse!

49
00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.980
[FAMILY MEN]
He did it!

50
00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:46.120
You made it, Gomorrah!

51
00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:48.830
[MARINE]
All units!

52
00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:52.460
The King Bull carrying the
pirates broke through Block D

53
00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:53.560
<b>Courthouse</b>

54
00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.560
<b>Tower of Justice</b>

55
00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.590
and they are now at
the Courthouse Plaza!

56
00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:55.730
I repeat!

57
00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:59.100
The King Bull carrying
the pirates broke through...

58
00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:03.460
[SPANDAM]
Look at this, Funkfreed.

59
00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.420
[SPANDAM]
A Golden Transponder Snail.

60
00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:11.350
Having this little gadget is the same

61
00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:14.420
as having the authority
to issue a Buster Call.

62
00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:17.660
That means I have the
same power as a Navy admiral,

63
00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:20.930
or someone even higher up than that!

64
00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:23.270
Admiral Aokiji entrusted it to me.

65
00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:26.140
The question is
"if and when will I use it"?

66
00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:30.010
Just you wait!

67
00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:32.010
Once I revive the ancient weapons,

68
00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:34.980
this won't just be something
that's "on loan" to me.

69
00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:39.940
I'll carry it of my own accord,
along with the power to control an army.

70
00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:49.410
[SPANDAM]
With the single push of a button,
an entire island will disappear!

71
00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:53.180
Authority can be a weapon unto itself.

72
00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.650
Oh, the power.

73
00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:57.220
[OFFICIAL]
Chief Spandam!

74
00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:58.720
[SPANDAM]
That was close!

75
00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:01.020
What's wrong with you?

76
00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:03.080
Can't you even knock?

77
00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:05.120
I almost accidentally hit the button!

78
00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:06.850
I'm terribly sorry, sir!

79
00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:09.450
But I'm afraid we've
got an emergency here!

80
00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:12.920
There's an urgent call from
Enies Lobby's Main Island!

81
00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:14.090
Idiots!

82
00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:17.570
If there's an emergency, why didn't
they just call my room directly?

83
00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:18.530
What the...?

84
00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:19.370
Hey!

85
00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:20.570
Why is the receiver off the hook?

86
00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:22.100
This always happens!

87
00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:24.040
Who's responsible?

88
00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:27.510
Well, either way, you were saying
something about an emergency, weren't you?

89
00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:29.310
[OFFICIAL]
Yes sir!

90
00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.040
Spanda.

91
00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:47.250
[SPANDAM]
Hey! Ms. Robin!

92
00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.400
It seems we have an
urgent report coming in

93
00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.900
from the marines
down at the Main Island.

94
00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:58.540
Knowing what it's likely about,
I wouldn't call it an "emergency," exactly.

95
00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:03.850
Your friends tried their best but only
managed to take down five of our soldiers.

96
00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:06.450
I wonder how they
were ultimately defeated.

97
00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:08.550
Did some of my other
men bring them down,

98
00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:12.460
or was it the giant gatekeeping
team of Oimo and Kashii?

99
00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:14.620
So many possibilities.

100
00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:17.550
Why don't we listen to the
report about these idiots

101
00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:22.390
who defied the World Government
and learn their fate together?

102
00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:23.660
You're such a scumbag.

103
00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:25.660
[SPANDAM]
Shut up, you low-life!

104
00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:30.960
[SPANDAM]
This is Spandam.

105
00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:33.810
I understand you have a report?

106
00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:34.710
Chief Spandam!

107
00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:35.880
Finally! Thank goodness.

108
00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:38.530
I tried your direct line,
but I couldn't get through!

109
00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:41.620
I'm... I'm not really
sure where to begin.

110
00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:42.910
[SPANDAM]
Calm down!

111
00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:43.610
Take it easy.

112
00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:45.320
It's the Straw Hats, right?

113
00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:46.940
Yes, what about them?

114
00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:47.590
Whoa!

115
00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:48.290
Hold on!

116
00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:49.250
Listen.

117
00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:51.910
Just pick up from where
your last report ended.

118
00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:54.820
Give me the gritty
details loudly and clearly.

119
00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:55.520
Right!

120
00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:57.890
[OFFICIAL]
The intruders... [SPANDAM (OVER SNAIL)]
Did you accidentally kill them?

121
00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:58.850
Pity.

122
00:07:58.850 --> 00:07:59.850
It's their fault for
being such weaklings.

123
00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:03.150
The intruders consist
of about sixty pirates!

124
00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:05.480
They've pushed their way all
the way through the Main Island

125
00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:07.320
and have reached the Courthouse Plaza!

126
00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:10.130
We can't stop them, sir!

127
00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:17.590
[MARINE]
All personnel on
Enies Lobby's Main Island!

128
00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:20.590
Head to the Courthouse
Plaza immediately!

129
00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.680
[ZAMBAI]
You did a good job, Gomorrah!

130
00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:30.450
I swear, everything you
two did will not be in vain!

131
00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.480
All right, we're breaking in!

132
00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:36.250
It's time to save Big Bro Franky!

133
00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:38.750
[FAMILY MEN]
Yeah!

134
00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:43.490
I repeat: The pirates have
reached the Courthouse Plaza!

135
00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:04.950
Can you see Luffy?

136
00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:12.470
Nope.

137
00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:14.400
[SANJI]
But whether he's up on the roof or not,

138
00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.340
it's not exactly like we
can just jump up after him.

139
00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:18.240
[ZORO]
That's true.

140
00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:21.230
Not much we can do.

141
00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:23.770
How many members of CP9
did you see up there?

142
00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:27.970
It was just that one
big guy with the bull horns.

143
00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:34.470
[SANJI]
It's hard to believe that Robin, Franky,
all of them, are right behind those doors.

144
00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:36.640
In any case, we need
to catch up with Luffy!

145
00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:38.640
Then we can save Robin together!

146
00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:39.340
[MARINE]
Hurry!

147
00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:40.640
Get to the Courthouse!

148
00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.240
[MARINE]
The drawbridge isn't down yet!

149
00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:43.350
Corner them!

150
00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:57.530
[YOKOZUNA]
Gero!

151
00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:05.350
[FAMILY MAN]
Whoa!

152
00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:06.950
That frog's awesome!

153
00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:09.340
[FAMILY MAN]
That's the same ball
that took out Gomorrah!

154
00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:10.870
Who threw it?

155
00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:14.530
Look!

156
00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:15.700
There're three of them!

157
00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.400
And they're running away!

158
00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:18.740
Why are they running away?

159
00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:20.510
They're the ones that attacked first!

160
00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:21.100
Idiot cook!

161
00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:23.300
We can't go chasing around every
enemy that runs off like that!

162
00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:25.580
It's a waste of time!

163
00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:42.740
Oh, pipe down.

164
00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.380
It's confirmation.

165
00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:48.420
Some of them need to
be chased, understand?

166
00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:50.990
To find out who we're up against.

167
00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.480
[FAMILY MAN]
That was amazing!

168
00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:55.350
[FAMILY MAN]
Who is this guy?

169
00:10:55.350 --> 00:10:56.820
[FAMILY MAN]
He must have superhuman strength

170
00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:58.490
to swing something like that around!

171
00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:02.540
[FAMILY MAN]
You think he's part of some special
unit, like those guard dogs?

172
00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.620
There're probably more of them
hiding out there somewhere.

173
00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:07.090
Let's be careful.

174
00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:10.480
We need to get moving.

175
00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.690
It looks like the
reinforcements have arrived.

176
00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.160
[MARINE]
Surround them!

177
00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:16.790
There's no way they'll be able
to open those heavy stone doors!

178
00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:18.080
We'll have them cornered!

179
00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:19.880
Move it!

180
00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:20.950
He's right!

181
00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:23.910
Now that I think about it, how...

182
00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.640
– are we gonna open...

183
00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:30.340
– those big, stone...

184
00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:33.600
[ZORO]
We're going in first!

185
00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:35.370
Stay close... don't fall behind!

186
00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:39.470
He... He cut right through
them, like it was nothing!

187
00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:40.900
[MOZU]
Hey! Zambai!

188
00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:41.830
Let's split up!

189
00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:43.770
We need to charge
both of those towers...

190
00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:46.570
– 'Cuz each side has a lever
to open up that drawbridge.

191
00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:47.170
Yeah!

192
00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:47.910
Good thinking!

193
00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:49.050
I'm on it!

194
00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:50.050
Right!

195
00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:52.620
Looks like we need to
split into three teams!

196
00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:54.380
Most of you go with Kiwi and Mozu!

197
00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:55.350
The rest are with me!

198
00:11:55.350 --> 00:11:57.750
We'll crack some heads
in that courthouse!

199
00:11:57.750 --> 00:11:59.450
Good luck, everyone.

200
00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:00.490
Move!

201
00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:12.040
<b>Courthouse</b>
<b>Tower of Justice</b>

202
00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:13.680
Huh?

203
00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:16.550
[MARINE (OVER SNAIL)]
Also, the gatekeepers of
the Main Island Front Gate,

204
00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:19.360
Oimo and Kashii, have
joined up with the pirates!

205
00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:22.640
They're currently destroying the central part
of the Main Island!

206
00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.980
[CASHY]
Get outta the way!

207
00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:31.120
[MARINE (OVER SNAIL)]
After hearing all the field reports,

208
00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:35.890
our guard casualties total
must be over 2,000 men!

209
00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:36.590
Wait.

210
00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:37.560
Not five?

211
00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:40.330
[MARINE (OVER SNAIL)]
And the man who took down
over a thousand of those men

212
00:12:40.330 --> 00:12:44.470
all by himself, the notorious Straw
Hat Luffy, has suddenly disappeared!

213
00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:47.010
We're still assessing
the situation here!

214
00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:51.440
In the history of this island,
this is, without a doubt, the

215
00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:54.750
absolute worst thing that has
ever happened at Enies Lobby!

216
00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:02.420
[SPANDAM]
It's Blueno!

217
00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:04.420
What's he doing out
there on that rooftop?

218
00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.270
What's happening here?

219
00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:11.040
And why now?

220
00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:15.480
What the hell's going on?

221
00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:18.400
[SPANDAM (OVER SNAIL)]
Baskerville!

222
00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:20.300
Chief Justice Baskerville!

223
00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:21.900
Come in! It's me!

224
00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:24.870
[LEFT & RIGHT BASKERVILLE]
Oh! Hello, Chief Spandam!

225
00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:24.660
<b>Courthouse</b>

226
00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:27.010
[LEFT BASKERVILLE]
This is Left Baskerville on the left!

227
00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:29.070
[RIGHT BASKERVILLE]
This is Right Baskerville on the right.

228
00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:30.530
[CENTER BASKERVILLE]
And located in the center,

229
00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:34.330
it is none other than I...Central
Freeway, closed for repairs!

230
00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:35.730
Shut up!

231
00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:37.700
[SPANDAM (OVER SNAIL)]
Just give me a status report, damn it!

232
00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:41.670
Is it true that the intruders have
made it to the courthouse plaza or not?

233
00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:43.210
Let's see.

234
00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:46.020
A status report, huh?

235
00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:50.550
That's a tricky one.

236
00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:54.420
[RIGHT BASKERVILLE]
They're not so much in the plaza
as they are inside the courthouse.

237
00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:56.150
[BASKERVILLE]
It's just awful!

238
00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:57.390
[SPANDAM (OVER SNAIL)]
What?

239
00:14:03.850 --> 00:14:04.550
Chief!

240
00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:05.710
Chief Justice!

241
00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:06.610
I have a report!

242
00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:11.300
The pirates have cut through our
defenses and broken down the front door.

243
00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:14.320
They're currently
inside the courthouse.

244
00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:16.150
[BASKERVILLE]
We can see that already, fool!

245
00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:18.590
Not as much resistance as I expected.

246
00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:20.760
We should be able
to tear right through.

247
00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:22.660
Wait, what's that?

248
00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:26.800
[FAMILY MAN]
Whoa, what? He's got 3 heads!

249
00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:30.200
[FAMILY MAN]
He's just like that dog
that guards the underworld!

250
00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:30.900
[FAMILY MAN]
Berberus?

251
00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:32.310
You mean "Cerberus"!

252
00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:34.310
[CENTER BASKERVILLE]
Order in the court, damn it!

253
00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:37.250
This is a sacred chamber
of law, you hooligans!

254
00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:42.390
You had the nerve to burst in here so shut
up, sit still and receive your sentence!

255
00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:44.120
[YOKOZUNA]
Gero!

256
00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:49.030
[ZAMBAI]
All right guys, you head to the
roof and join up with Straw Hat.

257
00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:52.890
We'll stay here at the door with
Yokozuna and hold off the Marines.

258
00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:56.710
We'll watch your back, so keep moving
and don't worry about the small fries!

259
00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:57.510
Gero!

260
00:14:57.510 --> 00:14:58.380
You got it.

261
00:14:58.380 --> 00:15:01.210
[NAMI]
Hey, it looks like they're starting
some kind of trial over there.

262
00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.010
Hm?

263
00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:02.670
Who cares?

264
00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:03.800
Just ignore them.

265
00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:04.730
Which way do we go?

266
00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:05.430
[NAMI]
Straight ahead!

267
00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:07.410
There are stairs on both sides.

268
00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:08.750
Let's make our way to the top!

269
00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:09.750
Right.

270
00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:10.450
Hey!

271
00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:12.210
They're ignoring the trial!

272
00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:15.210
I know they're pirates, but seriously,
how rude can these guys get!

273
00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:16.060
Bastards!

274
00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.280
How dare you mock the judicial island!

275
00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:20.250
I'll teach you some respect!

276
00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:26.210
Are his swords bending,
or am I seeing things?

277
00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:29.740
[ZORO]
Charming Demon.

278
00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.110
Sleepless Night.

279
00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.050
Onigiri!

280
00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:44.860
Is he the guy who broke the door?

281
00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.340
Well, that's that.

282
00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:49.770
Now let's get moving!

283
00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:51.110
Right!

284
00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:56.830
[FAMILY MAN]
He puts all of us to shame and he's
not even the captain of their crew!

285
00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:58.630
[SANJI]
Hey hey hey, wait!

286
00:15:58.630 --> 00:15:59.830
Outta the way, reindeer!

287
00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:00.930
Outta the way, Moss Head!

288
00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:02.170
I'm coming through!

289
00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:02.870
Hm?

290
00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:04.200
I forgot about him.

291
00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:06.450
Somebody's gotta protect Nami
from all of these bad guys

292
00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:09.760
and that somebody's
gonna be me, damn it!

293
00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:10.530
Now move!

294
00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.270
[ZORO]
Watch it!

295
00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:11.970
What?

296
00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:14.640
Why is he picking a fight now?

297
00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:16.640
[ZORO]
If you wanna settle
this, then bring it!

298
00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:18.210
Shut up!

299
00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:21.180
This is your fault for trying
to hog Nami all for yourself!

300
00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:22.050
Follow me, Nami.

301
00:16:22.050 --> 00:16:23.180
Forget about him.

302
00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:28.430
Uh, hey, we came to this place
to rescue Robin, remember?

303
00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:29.380
Oh!

304
00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:31.150
I bet she's waiting for me!

305
00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:33.160
She's waiting for
her prince to save her!

306
00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:35.890
She's probably crying right now,
'cause she misses me so much!

307
00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:37.060
Whatever!

308
00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:40.200
Hm? Come on!

309
00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:42.790
[NAMI]
Are you kidding me?

310
00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:43.890
[CHOPPER]
Come back, Zoro!

311
00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.320
That's the wrong way!

312
00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:46.750
You sure?

313
00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:47.820
How can you screw this up

314
00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:49.910
when the stairs are right
in front of your face?

315
00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:50.880
What's wrong with you?

316
00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:53.840
If you'd stop giving such crappy
directions, this wouldn't happen!

317
00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:56.750
[NAMI]
You are not blaming this on me!

318
00:16:56.750 --> 00:17:01.070
Zoro, I'll try to make you some medicine
later, to fix your brain problem.

319
00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:02.290
Brain problem?

320
00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:03.120
Hey, Chopper?

321
00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:03.990
Hm?

322
00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:06.620
[NAMI]
Make some for him while you're at it.

323
00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.220
I'll try, but he may be beyond help.

324
00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:12.380
[FAMILY MAN]
I'm starting to have doubts
about this whole rescue thing.

325
00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:14.380
[ZAMBAI]
They'll pull it together
when the going gets tough.

326
00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:15.580
I'm sure.

327
00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:17.550
I mean, probably.

328
00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:19.820
I mean, hopefully.

329
00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:21.870
[LEFT BASKERVILLE]
These are serious crimes.

330
00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:24.370
[RIGHT BASKERVILLE]
Yes, they're quite grave indeed.

331
00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:29.210
[CENTER BASKERVILLE]
But we should show restraint
and sentence them to death!

332
00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:30.640
[LEFT & RIGHT BASKERVILLE]
Agreed!

333
00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:34.960
[BASKERVILLE]
Think you can ignore
the Chief Justice, huh?

334
00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:50.640
[ZORO]
Chopper. Nami.

335
00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:51.680
Go on ahead.

336
00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:55.980
I'll make quick work of this thing
and catch up with you in a second.

337
00:17:55.980 --> 00:17:56.880
Oh.

338
00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:58.750
I'm a "thing" now, am I?

339
00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:00.650
And easy to defeat, no less?

340
00:18:00.650 --> 00:18:03.660
I'll teach you the meaning
of fear, you little...

341
00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:05.980
[FAMILY MEN]
Pull!

342
00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:11.400
[BASKERVILLE]
No! Stop it!

343
00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:15.530
[FAMILY MEN]
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

344
00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:17.950
[BASKERVILLE]
No.

345
00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:30.470
You gotta go through
us first, Cerberus!

346
00:18:30.470 --> 00:18:32.370
Are you sure about this?

347
00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:34.090
Let's go.

348
00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.890
Uh, right!

349
00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:41.020
<b>Luffy vs. Blueno
Courthouse Rooftop</b>

350
00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:51.580
[LUFFY]
Finally!

351
00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:52.680
My face closed!

352
00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:53.820
Of course.

353
00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.390
All open doors will eventually shut.

354
00:18:56.390 --> 00:19:00.360
I'm amazed you still managed
to dodge my Tempest Kick.

355
00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:01.760
[LUFFY]
Yeah. No big deal.

356
00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:03.590
[BLUENO]
How unsettling.

357
00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:08.040
[LUFFY]
Jerk!

358
00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:11.280
He's fast!

359
00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:15.050
[BLUENO]
Finger Pistol!

360
00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:16.920
Shave!

361
00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:18.020
Iron Body!

362
00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:20.060
Strong!

363
00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:23.140
[LUFFY]
Now Gum Gum...

364
00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:24.540
Bullet!

365
00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:25.880
Iron Body!

366
00:19:30.150 --> 00:19:31.510
Tempest Kick!

367
00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:45.700
[BLUENO]
He's completely keeping
up with my speed.

368
00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:49.340
He even changed the
course of my Tempest Kick!

369
00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:53.240
His physical abilities
are unbelievable.

370
00:19:54.310 --> 00:19:55.880
[LUFFY]
It's no good.

371
00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:58.600
I can't stay like this.

372
00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:00.070
It won't work.

373
00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:03.940
When I lost to Aokiji,
I realized something.

374
00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:05.680
I said to myself.

375
00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:08.960
"You keep running into guys
that are stronger and stronger.

376
00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:13.790
Unless you can get stronger too,
you can't protect your friends."

377
00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:15.730
And I want to.

378
00:20:16.390 --> 00:20:18.360
They're not all strong like me.

379
00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:21.690
But either way, they're my
friends and I wanna keep 'em,

380
00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:23.800
so I have to get
stronger than anyone else.

381
00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:27.040
Otherwise there's a
chance I could lose them.

382
00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.770
[BLUENO]
Then what are you gonna do?

383
00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:33.210
[LUFFY]
I thought of a new way
to fight with all my might,

384
00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:36.750
so that I won't lose anyone.

385
00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:41.960
So I won't let anyone
slip away from me.

386
00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:42.990
[BLUENO]
What's happening to him?

387
00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:45.980
What's going on inside his body?

388
00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:51.700
[LUFFY]
That did it.

389
00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:53.900
You won't be able to stop me now.

390
00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:55.640
What?

391
00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:57.650
All my strength and techniques just

392
00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:59.300
just went up by one step.

393
00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:04.220
Second Gear!
